# Testing & Quality Assurance

## Testing Strategy

### Test Pyramid
- **Unit Tests**: Test individual components and methods in isolation
- **Integration Tests**: Test component interactions and API endpoints
- **Feature Tests**: Test complete user workflows and business processes
- **End-to-End Tests**: Test full application flows

```php
// Good: Test pyramid structure
// Unit Test - Service method
public function test_course_service_creates_course()
{
    $data = ['title' => 'Test Course', 'description' => 'Test Description'];
    $course = $this->courseService->createCourse($data);
    
    $this->assertInstanceOf(Course::class, $course);
    $this->assertEquals('Test Course', $course->title);
}

// Integration Test - API endpoint
public function test_course_api_returns_courses()
{
    Course::factory()->count(3)->create();
    
    $response = $this->getJson('/api/courses');
    
    $response->assertStatus(200)
             ->assertJsonCount(3, 'data');
}

// Feature Test - Complete workflow
public function test_user_can_enroll_in_course()
{
    $user = User::factory()->create();
    $course = Course::factory()->published()->create();
    
    $this->actingAs($user)
         ->post("/courses/{$course->id}/enroll")
         ->assertRedirect()
         ->assertSessionHas('success');
         
    $this->assertDatabaseHas('course_enrollments', [
        'user_id' => $user->id,
        'course_id' => $course->id,
    ]);
}
```

## Laravel Testing Patterns

### Feature Testing
- Test complete user workflows
- Use database transactions for test isolation
- Mock external services
- Test authentication and authorization

```php
// Good: Feature test example
class CourseEnrollmentTest extends TestCase
{
    use RefreshDatabase;

    public function test_student_can_enroll_in_published_course()
    {
        $student = User::factory()->student()->create();
        $course = Course::factory()->published()->create();
        
        $this->actingAs($student)
             ->post("/courses/{$course->id}/enroll")
             ->assertRedirect()
             ->assertSessionHas('success');
             
        $this->assertDatabaseHas('course_enrollments', [
            'user_id' => $student->id,
            'course_id' => $course->id,
        ]);
    }

    public function test_student_cannot_enroll_in_draft_course()
    {
        $student = User::factory()->student()->create();
        $course = Course::factory()->draft()->create();
        
        $this->actingAs($student)
             ->post("/courses/{$course->id}/enroll")
             ->assertStatus(403);
             
        $this->assertDatabaseMissing('course_enrollments', [
            'user_id' => $student->id,
            'course_id' => $course->id,
        ]);
    }

    public function test_instructor_can_create_course()
    {
        $instructor = User::factory()->instructor()->create();
        
        $courseData = [
            'title' => 'Test Course',
            'description' => 'Test Description',
            'price' => 99.99,
        ];
        
        $this->actingAs($instructor)
             ->post('/courses', $courseData)
             ->assertRedirect()
             ->assertSessionHas('success');
             
        $this->assertDatabaseHas('courses', [
            'title' => 'Test Course',
            'instructor_id' => $instructor->id,
        ]);
    }
}
```

### Unit Testing
- Test individual methods and classes
- Mock dependencies properly
- Test edge cases and error conditions
- Use proper assertions

```php
// Good: Unit test example
class CourseServiceTest extends TestCase
{
    use RefreshDatabase;

    private CourseService $courseService;

    protected function setUp(): void
    {
        parent::setUp();
        $this->courseService = app(CourseService::class);
    }

    public function test_creates_course_with_valid_data()
    {
        $data = [
            'title' => 'Test Course',
            'description' => 'Test Description',
            'price' => 99.99,
            'instructor_id' => User::factory()->instructor()->create()->id,
        ];
        
        $course = $this->courseService->createCourse($data);
        
        $this->assertInstanceOf(Course::class, $course);
        $this->assertEquals('Test Course', $course->title);
        $this->assertEquals(99.99, $course->price);
    }

    public function test_throws_exception_for_invalid_data()
    {
        $this->expectException(ValidationException::class);
        
        $this->courseService->createCourse([]);
    }

    public function test_calculates_revenue_correctly()
    {
        $course = Course::factory()->create(['price' => 100]);
        $enrollments = CourseEnrollment::factory()->count(5)->create([
            'course_id' => $course->id,
            'amount_paid' => 100,
        ]);
        
        $revenue = $this->courseService->calculateRevenue($course);
        
        $this->assertEquals(500, $revenue);
    }
}
```

### Model Testing
- Test model relationships
- Test model scopes and methods
- Test model events and observers
- Test model validation

```php
// Good: Model test example
class CourseTest extends TestCase
{
    use RefreshDatabase;

    public function test_course_belongs_to_instructor()
    {
        $instructor = User::factory()->instructor()->create();
        $course = Course::factory()->create(['instructor_id' => $instructor->id]);
        
        $this->assertInstanceOf(User::class, $course->instructor);
        $this->assertEquals($instructor->id, $course->instructor->id);
    }

    public function test_published_scope_returns_only_published_courses()
    {
        Course::factory()->create(['status' => 'draft']);
        Course::factory()->create(['status' => 'published']);
        
        $publishedCourses = Course::published()->get();
        
        $this->assertCount(1, $publishedCourses);
        $this->assertEquals('published', $publishedCourses->first()->status);
    }

    public function test_slug_is_generated_from_title()
    {
        $course = Course::factory()->create(['title' => 'Test Course Title']);
        
        $this->assertEquals('test-course-title', $course->slug);
    }

    public function test_course_has_many_sections()
    {
        $course = Course::factory()->create();
        $sections = CourseSection::factory()->count(3)->create(['course_id' => $course->id]);
        
        $this->assertCount(3, $course->sections);
        $this->assertInstanceOf(CourseSection::class, $course->sections->first());
    }
}
```

## React Testing Patterns

### Component Testing
- Test component rendering
- Test user interactions
- Test component props
- Test component state

```tsx
// Good: Component test example
import { render, screen, fireEvent, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react';
import { CourseCard } from '@/components/course-card';
import { BrowserRouter } from 'react-router-dom';

const renderWithRouter = (component: React.ReactElement) => {
  return render(<BrowserRouter>{component}</BrowserRouter>);
};

describe('CourseCard', () => {
  const mockCourse = {
    id: '1',
    title: 'Test Course',
    description: 'Test Description',
    price: 99.99,
    instructor: { name: 'John Doe' },
  };

  it('should render course information', () => {
    renderWithRouter(<CourseCard course={mockCourse} />);
    
    expect(screen.getByText('Test Course')).toBeInTheDocument();
    expect(screen.getByText('Test Description')).toBeInTheDocument();
    expect(screen.getByText('$99.99')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it('should call onEnroll when enroll button is clicked', async () => {
    const onEnroll = jest.fn();
    renderWithRouter(<CourseCard course={mockCourse} onEnroll={onEnroll} />);
    
    fireEvent.click(screen.getByText('Enroll'));
    
    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(onEnroll).toHaveBeenCalledWith('1');
    });
  });

  it('should display loading state when enrolling', () => {
    renderWithRouter(<CourseCard course={mockCourse} isEnrolling={true} />);
    
    expect(screen.getByText('Enrolling...')).toBeInTheDocument();
    expect(screen.getByRole('button')).toBeDisabled();
  });
});
```

### Hook Testing
- Test custom hooks in isolation
- Mock dependencies properly
- Test hook return values
- Test hook state changes

```tsx
// Good: Hook test example
import { renderHook, act } from '@testing-library/react';
import { useModal } from '@/hooks/use-modal';

describe('useModal', () => {
  it('should initialize with closed state', () => {
    const { result } = renderHook(() => useModal());
    
    expect(result.current.isOpen).toBe(false);
    expect(result.current.data).toBe(null);
  });

  it('should open modal with data', () => {
    const { result } = renderHook(() => useModal());
    
    act(() => {
      result.current.open({ id: '1', name: 'Test' });
    });
    
    expect(result.current.isOpen).toBe(true);
    expect(result.current.data).toEqual({ id: '1', name: 'Test' });
  });

  it('should close modal', () => {
    const { result } = renderHook(() => useModal(true));
    
    act(() => {
      result.current.close();
    });
    
    expect(result.current.isOpen).toBe(false);
    expect(result.current.data).toBe(null);
  });
});
```

